//@ typecheck-fail
//@ requires: madaros
//@ error-pattern: modulo requires integer types
//@ description: Madaros rejects f64 `%=` with E050, exactly as it rejects `x = x % 2.0`
//
// Measured 2026-09-13: `x = x % 2.0` was rejected (E050) but `souc check`
// accepted `x %= 2.0`, because the compound-assign check typed the operator only
// through binary_result_type. Both checker paths now run the same operator-type
// check a written-out binary gets. lower_assign_stmt_ref also refuses f64 `%=`
// (no f64 rem lowering) in case a caller bypasses the checker.

fn main() with IO, Mut {
    var x = 5.5
    x %= 2.0
    println(x)
}
